Make the documentation readable straight from the filesystem.

font: false
  Drops the `fonts.googleapis.com` / `fonts.gstatic.com` stylesheet in favour
  of the system font stack.

navigation.instant
  Instant loading fetches pages over XHR, which browsers forbid for `file://`
  URLs.  The offline plugin refuses to run alongside it.

offline
  Emits the search index as JavaScript (the Fetch API is likewise unavailable),
  forces `use_directory_urls: false`, and rewrites the absolute paths that
  `site_url` would otherwise produce -- those resolve against the filesystem
  root and break every link and stylesheet.

MathJax is *not* patched here: it is vendored for both variants, so `mkdocs.yml`
already points at the local copy.

diff --git a/mkdocs.yml b/mkdocs.yml
index 09bca0b..f18c644 100644
--- a/mkdocs.yml
+++ b/mkdocs.yml
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@ use_directory_urls: false
 
 theme:
   name: material
+  font: false
   palette:
     - media: "(prefers-color-scheme: light)"
       scheme: default
@@ -27,8 +28,6 @@ theme:
     - content.code.copy
     - navigation.expand
     - navigation.indexes
-    - navigation.instant
-    - navigation.instant.progress
     - navigation.tabs
     - navigation.tabs.sticky
     - navigation.top
@@ -69,6 +68,7 @@ markdown_extensions:
 
 plugins:
 - search
+- offline
 - awesome-nav
 - gen-files:
     scripts:
